Solid ANSYS structural sim for **54_analysis** on cvbml02 (ws2), two plaque types **LAP** (low-attenuation) and **CP** (calcified), cases 500-999. Ported from the 65 sim (`pymapdl_simulation_ver5_fibrous.py`, PCG+OUTOFCORE+cell_sets patch) with paths only changed — see [[ansys-sim-cvbml02]], [[solid-dist-sim-cvbml01]].

**Scripts (on ws2 in `/home/jeff/project/54_analysis/`):**
- `pymapdl_sim_LAP.py` / `pymapdl_sim_CP.py` — differ only by `PLAQUE="LAP"|"CP"` constant in `__main__`.
- `run_plaque_batch.sh <LAP|CP>` — infinite resumable loop (pass + 90s sleep), bracket-safe pkill, stops when `STOP_<PLAQUE>` file appears. Args: START=500 END=1000 NPROC=20.
- **LOW-ONLY, 2 cases at a time (2026-07-28, latest user request — supersedes peak‖low):** user said "peak 안 돌리고 low만, 두 케이스씩 각 nproc 20". Orchestrator (`__main__`) builds `eligible` = cases with mesh + low csv + no low vtk, then runs a **WORKER POOL of PARN=3** (2026-07-28: was fixed-groups, but one slow case blocked the whole group → switched to a pool that refills each slot the instant a case finishes). Each slot = a `pymapdl_solve_bc.py` subprocess (DIFFERENT case, bc=low, @nproc 20 = ~54 cores, `start_new_session=True` so it's a process-group leader). On finish/fail, `finalize()` **always** rmtrees `case_{i}/low` scratch + cdb (final vtk is in parent case dir). Safety: **per-case TIMEOUT=9000s** (2.5h) → `os.killpg` the whole group (python + MAPDL child) and skip, freeing disk; **disk guard MIN_FREE_GB=450** won't start a new case if free disk is low. Reason: huge meshes (e.g. case 569, 662MB) blow PCG in-core → out-of-core sparse-direct fallback → **~357GB `.DSPtri` scratch** and hours per case; the pool lets such a case grind in ONE slot without blocking the other two, and the timeout/disk-guard bound the damage. **DISK-RUNAWAY GOTCHA (2026-07-29): case 975 (1.5GB mesh) produced a >700GB out-of-core factor growing ~13GB/min → would fill disk BEFORE the 2.5h timeout (disk-guard only stops NEW spawns, not the running case). Had to manually killpg 975 + `mv LAP_mesh/solid_LAP_975.msh .TOOBIG_oom` to skip it, freeing 700GB. LESSON: meshes ≳1.5GB may be un-runnable here (out-of-core factor > disk). Monitor must watch per-case scratch: if a live case's `low/` scratch exceeds ~550GB OR disk free < ~250GB, killpg it and move its mesh aside (skip). Skipped: the 6 corrupt (540,601,653,664,666,754) + 975 (OOM). These need re-mesh or a bigger-RAM/in-core solve. Monitor orphan-scan is the backstop. 2×20 = 40 cores. Each case's solve_bc builds its own cdb in its `low_dir`. Ports: `_ports(ci)` low_port = 50200+ci%50 (two concurrent cases → different ci → different port); solve_bc retries launch 4× on bumped port. Done-criterion & donecnt now = **low vtk only** (wrapper + plaque_status updated). Cases 500-529ish already have peak+low from earlier; new cases get low only.
- **HISTORY/gotchas:** fixed ports 50052/50100 caused intermittent "MAPDL failed to start gRPC server" (TIME_WAIT) → fixed with rotating ports. RESTART GOTCHA: must kill `pymapdl_sim_{LAP,CP}.py` orchestrator too (not just wrapper+solve_bc+ansys) or a stale orchestrator keeps running OLD in-memory code → TWO orchestrators → two cases at once / old ports. Full-nuke list: `[r]un_plaque_batch [p]ymapdl_sim_LAP.py [p]ymapdl_solve_bc.py [a]nsys.e [a]nsys251`, verify 0, then ONE clean start. Benchmark (508): seq 1×@30=900s vs parallel 2×@15=~718s (~20%, not 2×). Each writes `FC_case_{i}_{bc}.vtk` to the case dir; after both land, scratch subdirs+cdb are rm'd. Benchmark (case 508): sequential @30 = 900s/case vs parallel @15 = ~718s (~20% faster, NOT 2× — nproc halving slows each solve ~1.9×). nproc=20 chosen as middle ground (40 cores total, fits 64).
