**Wall BC (critical):** `post_data/wall_no_hyperemia/{peak,low}/wall_{bc}_case_{i}.csv`, cols x,y,z,Tx,Ty,Tz,Pressure (col 7). **ws2 has NO route to harvey** — sync runs on the LOCAL box: `sync_wall_harvey.sh` (scratchpad), 60s loop rsync `--ignore-existing` harvey->local->ws2, no --delete.
**SYNC-HANG GOTCHA (2026-07-29): the sync rsync HUNG silently for ~5.5h** (dropped harvey ssh, no timeout) — process stayed ALIVE (`pgrep` true) but the sync.log froze and ws2 low-csv stalled at 304 while harvey had 531 (frontier 788), capping the batch's runnable at 54. Two bugs: (1) rsync had no timeout so a stuck ssh hangs forever; (2) the restart used `pgrep ... || launch` which is a NO-OP when a hung process is still detected. FIXES: added `timeout 300 rsync --timeout=120 -e "ssh -o ConnectTimeout=20 -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3"`; and ALWAYS kill-then-launch (never `|| launch`). Monitor must check the sync LOG IS FRESH (last line < ~5 min old), not just that the process is alive. Wall data is plaque-agnostic → same csv unlocks both LAP & CP case i. harvey fills sequentially from 500 (its own [[steady3d-nohyperemia-54analysis]] run). A case runs only when mesh + BOTH peak&low csv present, else skipped and retried next pass.

